THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The pipeline in this repository depends on the following third-party work.
None of it is vendored here — clone or install each separately. Each remains
under its own license and is the work of its own authors.

1. CLRerNet
   "CLRerNet: Improving Confidence of Lane Detection with LaneIoU"
   Hiroto Honda and Yusuke Uchida, WACV 2024
   https://github.com/hirotomusiker/CLRerNet
   Apache License 2.0

   Used for lane boundary detection. `clrernet/detect_video.py` in this
   repository is my own code written against their model and config; the
   model, training code and weights are theirs.

2. YOLOv11 / Ultralytics
   https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
   AGPL-3.0

   Used for vehicle detection. Note that AGPL-3.0 is a strong copyleft
   licence — if you deploy a network service built on it, that obligation
   reaches your own source. It is listed here so nobody is surprised by it.

3. CULane dataset
   https://xingangpan.github.io/projects/CULane.html
   Used for the pre-trained lane detection weights. Research use terms apply.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT IS MINE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything under `notebooks/`, `clrernet/detect_video.py`, the lane-change
decision rule, the `HomemadeStrongSORT` tracker, and the integration between
the three models.
